(1. ANALOGY \(first 2-3 lines\)) Tj
T*
(Path param = the house number. Without it the postman cannot find the house.) Tj
T*
(Query param = extra notes: "come in the evening, use the lift". Optional.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. PLAIN MEANING) Tj
T*
(Path = which thing. Query = how to filter, sort, or display that thing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. ONE URL) Tj
T*
(/products/7?currency=INR) Tj
T*
(7 = which product \(path\)) Tj
T*
(currency=INR = how to show the price \(query\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. TABLE \(only on vs / difference questions\)) Tj
T*
(Aspect | Path | Query) Tj
T*
(Where | /users/42 | /users?role=admin) Tj
T*
(Job | ID / name | filter, sort, page) Tj
T*
(Required | usually yes | no) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. CODE - short, runnable, in the languages above) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. MISTAKE) Tj
T*
(Do not put filters in the path \(/users/admin/sort/name\). Routes explode.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. REMEMBER) Tj
T*
(Path = WHAT. Query = HOW to filter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Analogy first, then code. Do not write a long lecture.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(==================================================) Tj
T*
(GOLD EXAMPLE - match this depth) Tj
T*
(==================================================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Question: Params vs Query Params define) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Think of a shop.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Path param = the stall number: Shop No. 7.) Tj
T*
(Without it you do not know which shop to enter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Query param = an extra request: "show red shirts, sort cheap to expensive".) Tj
T*
(Optional. You can still find the shop if you skip it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(URL:) Tj
T*
(GET /products/7?currency=INR) Tj
T*
(- 7 is the path \(which product\)) Tj
T*
(- currency=INR is the query \(how to show the price\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Aspect | Path params | Query params) Tj
T*
(Place | /products/7 | /products?sort=price) Tj
T*
(Meaning | which thing | filter / sort / page) Tj
T*
(Required | yes | no) Tj
T*
(Example | /users/42 | /users?q=ram&page=2) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
